{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrrUZhVyNuAfQqeGNrCd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EQhwKzajG9DuhsmWQ1Ja5i","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat docs/adr/ADR-010-preact-adapter-ownership-split.md; sed -n 1,80p test/ssr.ts; grep -n \"renderParts\\|PartsEl\\|strip-render\\|spawn\\|execFile\" test/ssr.ts | head -40; sed -n 1,40p test/types.ts; cat tsconfig*.json; ls node_modules | grep -i preact"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11321,"cache_read_input_tokens":57109,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11321},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"106ce310-aed3-4fb7-a285-935ac4c8488d","uuid":"dad9a9b7-87d1-4efc-8c36-0562ca4752b2","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:07:49.867Z","request_id":"req_011CgrrUZV6ttR7Ays4JUMPS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01EQhwKzajG9DuhsmWQ1Ja5i":{"command":"cat docs/adr/ADR-010-preact-adapter-ownership-split.md; sed -n 1,80p test/ssr.ts; grep -n \"renderParts\\|PartsEl\\|strip-render\\|spawn\\|execFile\" test/ssr.ts | head -40; sed -n 1,40p test/types.ts; cat tsconfig*.json; ls node_modules | grep -i preact"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EQhwKzajG9DuhsmWQ1Ja5i","type":"tool_result","content":"# ADR-010: Preact owns the host, the element owns its children\n\n**Date:** 2026-11-08\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n\n**Related:** [ADR-004][adr-004] (client size), [ADR-005][adr-005] and\n[ADR-009][adr-009] (render links and render support)\n\n## Context\n\n`../components` (`@substrate-system/components`) is moving its\ncomponents onto microtags, and they have to work inside Preact apps.\nThat covers a client-only Preact render and a Preact `hydrate` of a\nserver-rendered page. A microtags element placed in a Preact tree\nfails in both server cases.\n\nOn the server, Preact's `renderToString` emits an empty host, such as\n`<number-input min=\"1\"></number-input>`. Preact only knows the host\ntag. It does not know that the component has markup of its own, so\nthe page arrives without the component's input or buttons.\n\nIn the browser, Preact 10's `hydrate` collects every existing child of\nan element it hydrates and removes each child it has no vnode for. The\ncomponent's own markup has no vnode, so even if the server sent it,\n`hydrate` deletes it. The only exception is an element whose vnode has\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. Preact leaves that element's children alone.\n\nThe terms below have their `CONTEXT.md` meanings. **Hydration** is the\nintent: attaching behaviour to markup that already exists in the\ndocument. **Adopt** is the mechanism: walking markup against existing\nDOM and binding to it without creating nodes. A microtags element\nhydrates itself when its class is registered. The adapter's job is to\nkeep Preact from undoing that hydration. It does not adopt anything\nitself.\n\n## Decision\n\nAdd a `microtags/preact` entry that exports `toPreact(El, options?)`.\nIt returns a Preact component that renders the element's host tag.\nOwnership is split at the host:\n\n- Preact owns the host tag and its attributes.\n- The element owns the host's children.\n\n**On the server**, the adapter builds the host vnode from the\ncomponent's render parts (the `renderParts` static, ADR-009's render\nsupport behind a new registry key). The attributes come from the\nparts' `attrs`, and the parts' `html` goes in through\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML`. `renderToString` then produces the same\nmarkup as the component's own `render` static. A class whose render\nlink was stripped has no `renderParts`, so the adapter throws an error\nthat names the tag.\n\n**In the browser**, the adapter gives the host one shared, fixed\n`dangerouslySetInnerHTML` whose `__html` is the empty string. It also\npasses the declared props as vnode props, which Preact assigns as\nproperties because the host defines an accessor for each one. Mapped\nevents are passed as `on<event-name>` props. The mechanism depends on\ntwo branches of Preact's element diff:\n\n1. While hydrating, Preact neither writes `innerHTML` nor removes the\n   element's existing children. The server markup stays and the\n   element adopts it.\n2. Outside hydration, Preact writes `innerHTML` only when the new\n   `__html` differs from the old one. The value never changes, so it\n   is written at most once, on the first non-hydrating render. On a\n   client-only mount that write empties the host once, and the element\n   renders itself when it connects. Later renders never touch the\n   children.\n\nBoth branches were verified in Preact 10.29.7. The `preact` dev\ndependency is pinned, so a Preact change arrives as a deliberate bump,\nand the browser tests (hydrate keeps inner nodes, re-render keeps\nthem, typed input survives) check it.\n\nThe browser build is selected by a `browser` export condition, as\n`microtags/htm` already is, and never imports render support.\n\n## Rejected alternatives\n\n- **A bare host tag.** No adapter, just `<number-input>` in JSX. The\n  server output is an empty host, and `hydrate` deletes whatever\n  server children the host had. This is the problem itself.\n- **A global `options.vnode` hook.** One hook that recognises every\n  microtags tag and injects its inner HTML. It is implicit: a page\n  changes behaviour depending on whether some module installed the\n  hook. It is global, so it affects every Preact tree in the page,\n  and it runs on every vnode, not only microtags hosts.\n- **A per-call `__html` that changes with props.** Render the inner\n  HTML from the current props on every render. When a prop changes,\n  the new `__html` differs from the old, so Preact writes `innerHTML`\n  over live DOM. That replaces the element's nodes and destroys their\n  state: bindings, focus, and values the visitor typed.\n\n## Trade-offs\n\n- The approach depends on two internal branches of Preact's diff, not\n  a documented contract. The pin and the browser tests turn a silent\n  break into a failing bump.\n- **Props before definition.** If the element is not yet defined when\n  Preact first assigns a prop, the property does not exist on the\n  element, so Preact sets an attribute instead. The adapter does not\n  work around this. A component's declared props already read their\n  attribute at connect time, so the value still arrives. This ADR\n  records it as a known edge.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- No Preact children. The adapter does not accept them: passing them is\n  a type error, and the adapter throws in development. Slotting vnodes\n  into element-owned markup is out of scope.\n- The browser build of `microtags/preact` carries no render code. It\n  does not import render support, so with every render link stripped\n  a client bundle stays as small as ADR-004 requires.\n- `preact` is an optional peer dependency, like `typescript`. Core and\n  every entry other than `microtags/preact` never import it.\n- Render support gains a second registered function, the parts\n  function, under `Symbol.for('microtags.renderParts')`. ADR-009's\n  render record contract is unchanged, so any copy of core keeps\n  working with any copy of render support.\n\nNo ADR is superseded.\n\n[adr-004]: ./ADR-004-client-bundle-size-outranks-ergonomics.md\n[adr-005]: ./ADR-005-single-file-components-with-build-time-render-stripping.md\n[adr-009]: ./ADR-009-server-render-support-through-render-link.md\nimport { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process'\nimport {\n    mkdtempSync,\n    readFileSync,\n    rmSync,\n    writeFileSync,\n} from 'node:fs'\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os'\nimport { join, resolve } from 'node:path'\nimport { test } from '@substrate-system/tapzero'\nimport { signal, effect } from 'alien-signals'\nimport { define } from '../src/index.js'\nimport { transform } from '../src/build.js'\nimport {\n    coerceNumber,\n    coerceString,\n    coerceBoolean,\n    coerceJson,\n} from '../src/util.js'\n\n// These tests run under Node with no DOM (see `npm run test:ssr`).\n// They verify the server-side-rendering contract: microtags can define\n// components and expose the statics needed to build markup without a\n// browser. The component lifecycle (connect/setup/refs) is exercised by\n// the browser suite in test/index.ts.\n\ntest('SSR environment has no DOM globals', t => {\n    t.equal(typeof document, 'undefined', 'document is not defined')\n    t.equal(typeof HTMLElement, 'undefined', 'HTMLElement is not defined')\n    t.equal(\n        typeof customElements,\n        'undefined',\n        'customElements is not defined'\n    )\n})\n\ntest('define().setup() works without a DOM', t => {\n    // A throw here (e.g. touching HTMLElement/customElements) fails the\n    // test. setup never runs server-side (nothing connects), but its body\n    // must still load at define time without a browser.\n    const El = define('ssr-widget')\n        .withProps(p => ({ start: p.number() }))\n        .withRefs(r => ({ display: r.one(), inc: r.one() }))\n        .setup(ctx => {\n            const count = signal(ctx.props.start())\n            effect(() => { count() })  // track the signal\n        })\n\n    t.ok(El, 'defining a component returns the element class')\n})\n\ntest('element class exposes TAG and refs as statics', t => {\n    const El = define('ssr-counter')\n        .withProps(p => ({ start: p.number() }))\n        .withRefs(r => ({ display: r.one(), inc: r.one(), dec: r.one() }))\n        .setup(() => {})\n\n    t.equal(El.TAG, 'ssr-counter', 'TAG is the registered tag name')\n    t.deepEqual(\n        { ...El.refs },\n        { display: 'display', inc: 'inc', dec: 'dec' },\n        'refs maps each declared key to its own data-ref name'\n    )\n})\n\ntest('render link: class exposes render function and props list', t => {\n    const El = define('ssr-render-basic')\n        .withProps(p => ({\n            count: p.number(),\n            label: p.string(),\n        }))\n        .withRefs(r => ({ display: r.one() }))\n        .render(({ refs, children }) => {\n            return `<span data-ref=\"${refs.display}\">${children}</span>`\n        })\n        .setup(() => {})\n\n    t.equal(\n        typeof El.render,\n        'function',\n1:import { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process'\n93:    const code = spawnSync('npx', [\n97:    const out = spawnSync('node', [], { input: code, encoding: 'utf8' })\n103:    t.ok(parts.startsWith('threw: '), 'renderParts throws')\n105:        'the renderParts error names the support module')\n455:const PartsEl = define('ssr-parts')\n492:test('renderParts: assembled parts equal render byte for byte', t => {\n493:    const parts = PartsEl.renderParts(partsProps, partsOpts)\n497:        PartsEl.render(partsProps, partsOpts),\n501:        assembleParts(PartsEl.renderParts({ n: 1 } as typeof partsProps)),\n502:        PartsEl.render({ n: 1 } as typeof partsProps),\n507:test('renderParts: attrs hold declared props, then valid extra attrs', t => {\n508:    const { attrs } = PartsEl.renderParts(partsProps, partsOpts)\n521:test('renderParts: a true boolean is the empty string', t => {\n522:    const { attrs } = PartsEl.renderParts(partsProps, partsOpts)\n526:test('renderParts: a class with no render link has no renderParts', t => {\n530:    t.ok(!('renderParts' in Plain), 'defined without a render link')\n533:    const src = readFileSync('test/fixtures/strip-render.ts', 'utf8')\n541:        'typeof Counter.renderParts, typeof Counter.render, Counter.TAG)')\n542:    const code = spawnSync('npx', [\n546:    const ran = spawnSync('node', [], { input: code, encoding: 'utf8' })\n550:        'the stripped class has neither renderParts nor render')\nimport { define } from '../src/index.js'\nimport { refsDSL } from '../src/builders.js'\nimport { html, type Markup } from '../src/htm.js'\nimport type {\n    RefsMap,\n    SingleRefDef,\n    MultipleRefDef,\n    TypedEvent,\n} from '../src/types.js'\nimport type {\n    Signal as PublicSignal,\n    Serialized as PublicSerialized,\n    RenderParts as PublicRenderParts,\n} from 'microtags'\nimport { bindProp } from 'microtags'\nimport { signal, computed } from 'alien-signals'\n\n/**\n * Compile-time assertions for the typed-refs feature. This file is never\n * executed or bundled into the runtime suite; it is type-checked by\n * `npm run typecheck` and exists purely to gate the ref type behaviour.\n */\n\n// Type-level equality helpers (the standard Equal / Expect pattern).\ntype Equal<X, Y> =\n    (<T>() => T extends X ? 1 : 2) extends\n    (<T>() => T extends Y ? 1 : 2) ? true : false\ntype Expect<T extends true> = T\n\n// RefsMap maps a single marker to its element type.\ntype _mapDisplay = Expect<Equal<\n    RefsMap<{ display:SingleRefDef<HTMLDivElement> }>['display'],\n    HTMLDivElement\n>>\n\n// An un-annotated single marker defaults to HTMLElement.\ntype _mapDefault = Expect<Equal<\n    RefsMap<{ host:SingleRefDef }>['host'],\n    HTMLElement\n>>\n{\n    \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.json\",\n    \"compilerOptions\": {\n        \"rootDir\": \"./src\",\n        \"ignoreDeprecations\": \"6.0\"\n    },\n    \"exclude\": [\n        \"example\",\n        \"example-hydration\",\n        \"test\",\n        \"src/cli.ts\"\n    ]\n}\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"listFiles\": true,\n    \"module\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"Bundler\",\n    \"esModuleInterop\": false,\n    \"ignoreDeprecations\": \"6.0\",\n    \"lib\": [\"ES2022\", \"DOM\", \"WebWorker\", \"dom.iterable\"],\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"allowJs\": false,\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"outDir\": \"dist\",\n    \"allowSyntheticDefaultImports\": true,\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"emitDecoratorMetadata\": true,\n    \"strict\": true,\n    \"sourceMap\": true,\n    \"forceConsistentCasingInFileNames\": true,\n    \"resolveJsonModule\": true,\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"noImplicitAny\": false,\n    \"declaration\": true,\n    \"declarationDir\": \"dist\",\n    \"declarationMap\": true\n  },\n  \"include\": [\n    \"example\",\n    \"example-hydration\",\n    \"src/**/*\",\n    \"test\",\n    \"lib.es5.d.ts\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"extends\": \"./tsconfig.json\",\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"listFiles\": false,\n    \"customConditions\": [\"browser\"]\n  },\n  \"exclude\": [\"example/ssr.ts\", \"example-hydration/server\"]\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"106ce310-aed3-4fb7-a285-935ac4c8488d","uuid":"fc6154c5-ee37-4753-9b8d-e1b947a403a7","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:07:50.194Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# ADR-010: Preact owns the host, the element owns its children\n\n**Date:** 2026-11-08\n\n**Status:** Accepted\n\n**Related:** [ADR-004][adr-004] (client size), [ADR-005][adr-005] and\n[ADR-009][adr-009] (render links and render support)\n\n## Context\n\n`../components` (`@substrate-system/components`) is moving its\ncomponents onto microtags, and they have to work inside Preact apps.\nThat covers a client-only Preact render and a Preact `hydrate` of a\nserver-rendered page. A microtags element placed in a Preact tree\nfails in both server 