{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrrtjPaSgzjCnKZsq6ih","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm run gate` runs the new suite and passes.\n\nTicket 03 is finished. `microtags/preact` now has its full public type and the default (Node and SSR) build. `npm run gate` passes and includes the new suite, `test:preact-ssr`, with 15 assertions.\n\n**What's new:**\n- **`src/preact-shared.ts`** is the module both builds share. It holds the adapter's prop types: declared props (all optional), one callback per mapped event, the `class`/`id`/`aria-*`/`data-*` passthrough, and `children?:never`. It also has `splitProps`, which sorts incoming props into declared props, event handlers keyed by DOM event name, and passthrough attributes. It throws an error naming the tag if children are passed. It never imports render support, so ticket 04's browser build can use it.\n- **`src/preact.ts`** is the default build.\n  - It imports render support and builds the host vnode from `El.renderParts`. An empty-string value (a true boolean) becomes `true`, and the inner HTML goes in through `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`.\n  - Passthrough attributes go into `renderParts` as extra `attrs`. They get the same attribute-name filter as the `render` static and also reach the render function's `ctx.attrs`.\n  - A class with no `renderParts` throws when it is rendered, not when `toPreact` is called. The error names the tag and says to import the variant that keeps its render link.\n- **`package.json`:**\n  - A `./preact` export with `types`, `import` and `require`, and `src/preact.ts` added to `build-cjs` and `build-esm`.\n  - `preact` as an optional peer at `^10.29.7`.\n  - Dev dependencies: `preact` pinned to exactly `10.29.7`, and `preact-render-to-string` `^6.8.2`.\n  - The `test:preact-ssr` script, added to `gate` right after `test:ssr`.\n- **Tests:**\n  - `test/preact-ssr.ts` compares the host tag and a decoded attribute map, parsed with a small helper (no parser dependency), and compares the inner HTML as a string.\n  - `test/types.ts` imports from `'microtags/preact'`.\n- **Docs:** `AGENTS.md` has a short section on the adapter.\n\n**Things to know:**\n- **One test can't fail on its own code.** `preact-render-to-string` 6.8.2 already prints an empty-string attribute as a bare attribute. So removing the `'' -> true` step still passes the boolean test. I kept the step because the ticket asks for it.\n- **The other checks were confirmed by breaking the code:**\n  - Removing the event filter fails the callback test.\n  - Removing the children throw fails the children test.\n  - Loosening `children?:never` leaves its `@ts-expect-error` unused, so typecheck fails.\n- **Peer range:** I chose `^10.29.7` rather than any Preact version, because the browser side depends on Preact 10 diff behavior. Widen it if you'd rather not tie consumers to that.\n- **Untyped extra props:** any prop that isn't declared or a mapped event is passed through to the host at runtime. The types still reject anything other than `class`, `id`, `aria-*` and `data-*`.\n- **No-render-link test:** it covers a class defined without `.render()`. The stripped case looks the same at runtime, and ticket 01's test already checks that stripped classes have no `renderParts`.\n- `src/preact.ts` is not in `build-esm:min` and has no size entry yet; both arrive with the browser build in ticket 04.\n\nFive commits are on the branch. My notes for this attempt are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":161,"cache_read_input_tokens":98835,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":161},"output_tokens":761,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_